<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Kussara</h1><p class="st-meta">1780 BCE – 1650 BCE (approx.) · capital Kussara</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Kussara, the Anatolian kingdom of Pithana and Anitta, who forged the first large state of central Anatolia and paved the way for the Hittites.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Kussara was a city in central or eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> whose site is still unknown. In the 18th century BCE its king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pithana">Pithana</a> seized Nesa, the city of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kanesh">Kanesh</a>, and made it a second capital, launching the kingdom's rise.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anitta">Anitta</a> conquered <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/zalpa">Zalpa</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hattum">Hattus</a>, received the submission of the great king of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/purushanda">Purushanda</a>, and took that title himself. His deeds are told in the Anitta text, the oldest known text in the Hittite language. Anitta built temples to the storm god and his own god Siusummi and celebrated victories with hunts of wild animals.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anitta">Anitta</a> did not last long, but the Hittite royal line traced its origins to Kussara; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusili-i">Hattusili I</a> called himself a man of Kussara. His move to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusa">Hattusa</a> c. 1650 BCE marks the start of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kussara.jpg" alt="Kussara" width="320" height="265"><figcaption>Image: Near_East_topographic_map-blank.svg: Sémhur derivative work: Al-qamar · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KarumKanis.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1780 BCE – 1650 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kussara</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Pithana, Anitta</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Anatolian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hittite</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Turkey</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Kussara</dd></dl></aside></div>
